{
  "_notes": "Roster ladder in four tiers (starter / budget / mid / marquee). Starter = cheap plant-eaters, the classic opening move. Diets map 1:1 to food.json items: herbivore->plants, carnivore->meat, piscivore->fish. Entries sorted by shop_price. Existing v1 ids are preserved; some v1 prices/popularity were retuned to fit the ladder. M4: `biomes` is the live mechanic, derived from biome_affinity (first entry = preferred, the rest tolerated; single-affinity species were given one hand-picked tolerated biome so nothing is preferred-only unless it is a marquee `requires_preferred` species). Preferred: popularity x balance.biome.preferred_popularity and extra health regen. Tolerated: neutral. Anything else is the WRONG biome: popularity x wrong_popularity, health drifts down to wrong_health_floor, an unhappy badge and a ticker/digest warning. `requires_preferred: true` (Triceratops, Spinosaurus, Brachiosaurus, Tyrannosaurus) means the Dino Market and the enclosure picker refuse any pen that is not a preferred biome. Desert (cheapest land) is home to the small starters and the desert hunters; marsh to the duck-bills, Baryonyx and Spinosaurus; plains to most big herbivores.",
